{"folioDeck": 1, "exportedAt": "2026-11-12T00:00:00.000Z", "meta": {"id": "heabc", "title": "Hebrew Alphabet", "subtitle": "45 letters and signs · both directions, as two cards per letter", "desc": "The Hebrew alphabet: 45 notes, in the alphabet's order — the twenty-two letters, with the three that change their sound when a dot sits inside them taken one sound to a card (בּ b and ב v, כּ k and כ kh, פּ p and פ f) and shin and sin apart (שׁ sh, שׂ s); then the five final forms a letter takes at the end of a word (ך ם ן ף ץ); then the three letters with a geresh that spell borrowed sounds (ג׳ j, ז׳ zh, צ׳ ch); then the vowel points and the dagesh. The first deck of the Hebrew collection. Both directions: see a letter and recall its sound, or see a sound and recall the letter, each a card with its own schedule. Hebrew is written right to left, and its letters do not join. Everyday Hebrew is printed WITHOUT the vowel points — they appear in children's books, poetry, dictionaries and for learners — which is why the level decks print each word both ways, with a romanisation beneath. Every note gives the romanisation the level decks use, the sound described in English words, and one everyday word that shows it, pointed, with a speaker beside the letter and the word. Modern Hebrew says some letters alike — t for ט and ת, k for כּ and ק, v for ב and ו, kh for ח and כ, s for ס and שׂ, and nothing (or a catch in the throat) for א and ע — so the cards say which, and the sound side names the word it asks for, so every card has one answer. The sounds are those of modern Israeli Hebrew, approximated in English as every learner's alphabet does. Sources: the standard description of modern Israeli Hebrew; the example words' pointing and romanisations are English Wiktionary's, via the kaikki.org extraction (CC BY-SA 4.0).", "author": "", "language": "en", "color": "#5E6EC0", "tags": ["hebrew", "alphabet"], "glossMode": "site", "types": {"he-abc": {"id": "he-abc", "name": "Hebrew letter", "speechLang": "he-IL", "fields": ["Letter", "Name", "Shapes", "Sound", "Clue", "Example", "Word"], "cards": [{"name": "Letter → sound", "front": "<div class=\"uc-letter\">{{Letter}}<span class=\"uc-tts uc-say\" data-say=\"{{Name}}\"></span></div>{{#Shapes}}<div class=\"uc-shapes\">{{Shapes}}</div>{{/Shapes}}", "back": "{{FrontSide}}<hr><div class=\"uc-field\"><div class=\"uc-pos\">sound</div><div class=\"uc-gl\">{{Sound}}</div><div class=\"uc-pos uc-gap\">as in</div><div class=\"uc-gl\">{{Example}}<span class=\"uc-tts uc-say\" data-say=\"{{Word}}\"></span></div></div>"}, {"name": "Sound → letter", "front": "<div class=\"uc-ask\">Which letter is this?</div><div class=\"uc-field\"><div class=\"uc-gl\">{{Sound}}</div><div class=\"uc-pos uc-gap\">the letter in</div><div class=\"uc-gl\">{{Clue}}</div></div>", "back": "{{FrontSide}}<hr><div class=\"uc-letter\">{{Letter}}<span class=\"uc-tts uc-say\" data-say=\"{{Name}}\"></span></div>{{#Shapes}}<div class=\"uc-shapes\">{{Shapes}}</div>{{/Shapes}}<div class=\"uc-field\"><div class=\"uc-pos\">sound</div><div class=\"uc-gl\">{{Sound}}</div><div class=\"uc-pos uc-gap\">as in</div><div class=\"uc-gl\">{{Example}}<span class=\"uc-tts uc-say\" data-say=\"{{Word}}\"></span></div></div>"}], "css": ".card {\n  text-align: center;\n  font-size: 17px;\n  line-height: 1.6;\n}\n.uc-ask {\n  margin-bottom: 14px;\n  font-size: 11px;\n  letter-spacing: 0.14em;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  opacity: 0.55;\n}\n.uc-letter {\n  font-size: 64px;\n  font-weight: 400;\n  line-height: 1.3;\n}\n.uc-say {\n  margin-left: 14px;\n  vertical-align: middle;\n  font-size: 15px;\n}\n.uc-field {\n  display: block;\n  width: fit-content;\n  min-width: min(300px, 100%);\n  max-width: 100%;\n  margin: 14px auto 0;\n  padding: 11px 15px;\n  border: 1px solid var(--rule, rgba(0,0,0,0.12));\n  border-radius: 11px;\n  text-align: left;\n  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--paper-2, #EFEDE6) 58%, var(--card, #FFFFFF));\n}\n.uc-pos {\n  margin-bottom: 3px;\n  font-size: 9.5px;\n  letter-spacing: 0.14em;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  color: var(--ink-faint, #6C6A63);\n}\n.uc-gap {\n  margin-top: 10px;\n}\n.uc-gl {\n  line-height: 1.5;\n}\n.uc-rm {\n  font-weight: 600;\n}\n.uc-ex {\n  font-size: 21px;\n}\n.uc-exr {\n  margin-left: 6px;\n  font-size: 14px;\n  opacity: 0.62;\n}\n.uc-exe {\n  margin-left: 6px;\n  opacity: 0.62;\n}\n/* the letter's name, and its final form beneath it */\n.uc-shapes {\n  margin-top: 4px;\n  font-size: 15px;\n  opacity: 0.75;\n}\n.uc-fin {\n  margin-top: 2px;\n}\n.uc-sl {\n  margin-left: 5px;\n  font-size: 9.5px;\n  letter-spacing: 0.1em;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  opacity: 0.6;\n}\n.uc-sf {\n  margin-left: 8px;\n  font-size: 24px;\n  vertical-align: middle;\n}\n"}}, "version": 1, "createdAt": "2026-11-12T00:00:00.000Z", "updatedAt": "2026-11-12T00:00:00.000Z", "forkedFrom": null}, "cards": [{"sub": "", "fields": {"Letter": "<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">א</span>", "Name": "אָלֶף", "Shapes": "<div class=\"uc-sl\">alef</div>", "Sound": "<span class=\"uc-rm\">&#x27;</span> · no sound of its own: it carries the vowel that goes with it, or a light catch in the throat, as in the middle of uh-oh — said exactly as ע", "Clue": "<span class=\"uc-rm\">ába</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">father</span>", "Example": "<span class=\"uc-ex\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">אַבָּא</span><span class=\"uc-exr\">ába</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">father</span>", "Word": "אבא"}, "id": "u_heabc_1", "type": "he-abc"}, {"sub": "", "fields": {"Letter": "<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">בּ</span>", "Name": "בֵּית", "Shapes": "<div class=\"uc-sl\">bet</div>", "Sound": "<span class=\"uc-rm\">b</span> · &quot;b&quot; as in bed — ב with the dot (dagesh) inside it", "Clue": "<span class=\"uc-rm\">báyit</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">house</span>", "Example": "<span class=\"uc-ex\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">בַּיִת</span><span class=\"uc-exr\">báyit</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">house</span>", "Word": "בית"}, "id": "u_heabc_2", "type"